  "worked_solution": "Let's analyze each of the subsets.\n\n- The set $A$ is not a subspace because it does not contain the zero vector. Indeed, $0=\u27e80,0,0\u27e9$ does not satisfy the condition ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=1$ since ${0}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}\\ne 1.$\n\n- The set $B$ is not a subspace because it is not closed under vector addition. Indeed, both $a=\u27e81,0,1\u27e9$ and $b=\u27e80,1,1\u27e9$ belong to $B$ but \n\n$$\na+b=\u27e81,0,1\u27e9+\u27e80,1,1\u27e9=\u27e81,1,2\u27e9\n$$\n\n \ndoes not satisfy the condition $xyz=0$ since $1\\cdot 1\\cdot 2\\ne 0.$\n\n- The set $C$ is not a subspace because it does not contain the zero vector. Indeed, $0=\u27e80,0,0\u27e9$ does not satisfy the condition $y=-1$ since $0\\ne -1.$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"None.\"",
